## Mutual exclusivity: “Start with music” vs schedule category “Music”

These are mutually exclusive by design:
- If schedule category is `"Music"`, the schedule’s main `BiblePublicationSchedule` already points at a Music publication.
- Therefore `AlarmMusic` (“begin with music”) is disabled/cleared.

Enforced in two layers:
- `src/Bible.Alarm/Services/Schedule/ScheduleSaveService.cs`
  - when `BiblePublicationCategoryName == "Music"`:
    - forces `model.MusicEnabled = false`
    - sets `model.Music = null`
  - also clears music fields when mapping the saved model back to `ScheduleStateItem`
- `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Effects/Services/ScheduleEntityUpdater.cs`
  - if category is `"Music"`, it removes `existing.Music` even if present

