## Save persistence (what fields end up in Schedule DB)

### What gets saved for Bible selection

The schedule’s main content is persisted into Schedule DB tables:
- `AlarmSchedules` (time/days/name/flags)
- `BiblePublicationSchedules` (1:1)
  - `PublicationCode`
  - `LanguageCode` (nullable)
  - `SectionCode` (nullable)
  - `TrackNumber`
  - `FinishedDuration` reset is controlled by `biblePublicationUpdated`

### What gets saved for begin-with-music

Begin-with-music is stored as:
- `AlarmSchedules.MusicEnabled` (boolean)
- `AlarmMusic` (1:1) when enabled/selected
  - `MusicType`
  - `PublicationCode`
  - `LanguageCode` (vocal only)
  - `SectionCode` (for sectioned melody releases)
  - `TrackNumber`
  - `Repeat`

### The save path

- `ScheduleSaveService.PrepareModelForSave(...)` maps `ScheduleStateItem → AlarmSchedule`
  - applies the Category=Music rule (disable/clear begin-with-music)
  - ensures music entity is created/updated only when `musicUpdated` is true
- Effects persist:
  - `ScheduleEffects.HandleUpdateScheduleFromViewModel(shouldSave:true)`
  - uses `ScheduleEntityUpdater.UpdateScheduleEntity(...)` to merge into tracked EF entities

